course: dictionary
lesson: 283
title: Ammonia and the clues around it
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Ammonia is a noun, and it is uncountable: you say some ammonia, not two ammonias. It is a colourless gas with a very strong, sharp smell. The same word can also mean a liquid made when this gas dissolves in water, and that liquid is used in some cleaning products.
explain: Use the context to choose the right meaning. In «Many toilet cleaners are acids, and mixing bleach with ammonia cleaners makes other harmful gases», ammonia cleaners are cleaning products, so the liquid meaning fits. In «Jupiter's stripes are bands of clouds, light zones and darker belts, made of ammonia and other chemicals», ammonia is one of the chemicals in the clouds.
explain: Clue words can warn you of danger. The words «harmful» and «poisonous» show that some mixtures are not safe. Never mix cleaning products together, and always read the label first.
fact: Ammonia is a colourless gas with a very strong, sharp smell.
fact: Ammonia is made of nitrogen and hydrogen.
fact: An ammonia cleaner is a cleaning product that contains ammonia dissolved in water.
fact: Never mix ammonia cleaners with bleach, because the mixture gives off harmful gases.
fact: Farmers use fertilisers made from ammonia to help crops grow.
exercise: What is ammonia? | *A colourless gas with a very strong, sharp smell | A type of cloud that is always pink | A soft fruit that grows on trees | A bright light that shines in the night sky
exercise: «Never mix ammonia cleaners with bleach.» Why is this a safety rule? | The mixture makes the cleaner last longer | The mixture turns the bleach cold | The mixture makes the cleaner smell sweet | *The mixture can make harmful gases
exercise: The text says ammonia has a «very strong, sharp smell». Which two words describe the smell? | slow and gentle | soft and sweet | bright and loud | *strong and sharp
test: Ammonia is an uncountable noun. Which phrase is correct? | three ammonias | two ammonias | a few ammonias | *some ammonia
test: «Farmers use fertilisers made from ammonia to help crops grow.» What is ammonia used for in this sentence? | Keeping fish alive in tanks | Making bright lights for the night sky | *Making fertiliser that helps crops grow | Making soft, sweet fruit
exam: «Jupiter's stripes are bands of clouds, light zones and darker belts, made of ammonia and other chemicals.» What do the clues tell you about ammonia? | It is a kind of animal that lives on Jupiter | *It is one of the chemicals in Jupiter's clouds | It is the colour of Jupiter's sky | It is a tool for measuring the wind
